WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.169
When your shop misses a call, here is exactly what happens next.

00:00:05.569 --> 00:00:08.786
A customer with a broken air conditioner calls.

00:00:08.786 --> 00:00:11.594
Everyone is on a job, so nobody picks up.

00:00:11.594 --> 00:00:15.496
Normally, that customer calls the next company on Google.

00:00:16.896 --> 00:00:21.085
Instead, within seconds, they get this text: Sorry we missed your call.

00:00:21.085 --> 00:00:24.861
Reply with your address and a quick photo of what you need done.

00:00:26.261 --> 00:00:26.908
They reply.

00:00:26.908 --> 00:00:31.382
And you get their number, their message, and the photo, right on your phone.

00:00:31.382 --> 00:00:34.972
You call back from the truck, with the job already described.

00:00:36.372 --> 00:00:36.819
No app.

00:00:36.819 --> 00:00:38.095
No new phone number.

00:00:38.095 --> 00:00:41.670
I can handle the setup, and you can turn it off anytime.
